    "long_instructions": "**Is someone trying to steal your money?**\r\n\r\nPayment methods are rarely declined. One sign of fraud—such as a stolen credit card—is a lot of declined transactions. Use Python to analyze someone’s payment history for fraud.\r\n\r\n☑️ Do This:\r\n- Count the number of \"Approved\" and \"Declined\" purchases in the \"status\" column of `data.csv`.\r\n- Interpret the data: Is this payment method being used fraudulently? Be ready to share your thoughts on the next level.\r\n",
